AIM
To develop a simple server-side application using Node.js that creates a web server and responds to client requests.

PROGRAM
1. Install Node.js.
2. Create a file named 5.js and enter the following program.

const http = require("http");

// Create HTTP server
const server = http.createServer((request, response) => {

    // Set response header
    response.writeHead(200, {
        "Content-Type": "text/html"
    });

    // Send HTML response to client
    response.end(`
        <html>
        <head>
            <title>Node.js Server</title>
        </head>
        <body>
            <h1>Welcome to Node.js Server</h1>
            <p>This is a server-side application.</p>
        </body>
        </html>
    `);
});

// Start server on port 3000
server.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log("Server running at http://localhost:3000");
});

EXECUTION
1. Open Command Prompt or terminal in the folder containing 5.js.
2. Run the command:

node 5.js

3. Open a web browser and enter:

http://localhost:3000

OUTPUT
The terminal displays:
Server running at http://localhost:3000

The browser displays:
Welcome to Node.js Server
This is a server-side application.

RESULT
Thus, a server-side application was successfully developed using Node.js. The HTTP server accepts client requests and sends an HTML response.
